@@ -0,0 +1,83 @@
+# Self-hosting with Kamal
+
+The default [`config/deploy.yml`](../config/deploy.yml) deploys Fizzy to one Linux server. One app container runs Rails, Solid Queue background workers and recurring jobs, Solid Cache, and Solid Cable, all backed by SQLite. Uploads use local disk. A separate Kamal Proxy container obtains and renews a Let's Encrypt certificate and serves Fizzy over HTTPS.
+
+You do not need MySQL, Redis, S3, or the SaaS gem. Kamal uses a local registry on your development machine and forwards it to the server over SSH during deployment, so no registry account is needed.
+
+## Before you start
+
+- Fork and clone the repository. Install the Ruby version in `.ruby-version`, then run `bundle install`. Use the normal Gemfile, without enabling SaaS mode (`SAAS` or `tmp/saas.txt`).
+- Have Docker running on your development machine, with the Buildx plugin available, to build the image.
+- Prepare a Linux server with Docker and SSH key access. Kamal uses `root` by default; for another user, add `ssh: { user: your-user }` to the deployment config and give that user access to Docker.
+- Point your hostname's DNS A record (and AAAA record, if present) at the server. TCP ports 80 and 443 must be publicly reachable and available for Kamal Proxy. It needs direct access to obtain the certificate.
+- Have an SMTP server that the box can reach, credentials, and a sender address your mail provider permits. Email is required for sign-in codes and invitations.
+
+The default image is built for `amd64`. Change `builder.arch` to `arm64` if your server is ARM-based. Allow enough memory for old and new app containers to overlap during a deploy.
+
+## Configure your fork
+
+1. Edit `config/deploy.yml`:
+   - Replace `fizzy.example.com` next to `&host` with your hostname, **without** `https://`. The YAML alias reuses it for SSH, the proxy, and `APP_FQDN` (the hostname for links in mail and background jobs).
+   - Set `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS`, `SMTP_ADDRESS`, and your provider's port and authentication settings. `SMTP_DOMAIN` is the SMTP HELO domain; it defaults here to your Fizzy hostname.
+   - The example uses authenticated SMTP on port 587 with STARTTLS. See the alternatives below if your provider needs different settings.
+2. Create your private secrets file:
+
+   ```sh
+   cp .kamal/secrets.example .kamal/secrets
+   chmod 600 .kamal/secrets
+   bin/rails secret
+   ```
+
+   Put the generated value in `SECRET_KEY_BASE` in `.kamal/secrets`, and fill in `SMTP_USERNAME` and `SMTP_PASSWORD`. Generate the app secret **once** and keep it across deploys; changing it invalidates sessions and signed links. No Rails master key is needed for this setup.
+
+   `.kamal/secrets` is ignored by Git and excluded from Docker builds. Never put credentials in `config/deploy.yml` or commit them. You can reference exported environment variables in the secrets file instead of storing literal values. Single-quote literal passwords containing `$`, `#`, or spaces.
+3. From the repository root, check the config and deploy:
+
+   ```sh
+   bin/kamal config
+   bin/kamal setup
+   ```
+
+   Treat `kamal config` output as sensitive and do not publish it. `bin/kamal` uses the bundled version of Kamal; `bundle exec kamal setup` is equivalent.
+
+Kamal builds and starts the app and proxy. The image's entrypoint runs `db:prepare`, creating or migrating all four production SQLite databases. Visit `https://your-host` and sign up to create your first account. Verify that a sign-in email arrives.
+
+Kamal builds committed source by default. Commit any application changes you want deployed to your fork; keep secrets out of Git. Do not use the configs under `saas/`, which depend on 37signals' infrastructure.
+
+### Other mail servers
+
+- **Implicit TLS (usually port 465):** set `SMTP_PORT: 465` and add `SMTP_TLS: "true"` under `env.clear`. This disables STARTTLS to avoid mixing the two TLS modes.
+- **An unauthenticated relay:** set `SMTP_AUTHENTICATION: ""` and remove `SMTP_USERNAME` and `SMTP_PASSWORD` from `env.secret`. Use the relay's port. Set `SMTP_ENABLE_STARTTLS_AUTO: "false"` only if your trusted relay requires unencrypted SMTP.
+
+Boolean environment values must be quoted strings in the Kamal config. Web HTTPS is independent of SMTP TLS: leave `proxy.ssl` enabled and do not set `DISABLE_SSL`. Rails already assumes a TLS-terminating proxy and uses secure cookies.
+
+### Browser push notifications (optional)
+
+Generate a VAPID key pair once:
+
+```sh
+bundle exec ruby -rweb-push -e 'key = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{key.private_key}", "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{key.public_key}"'
+```
+
+Put both values in `.kamal/secrets` and uncomment their entries under `env.secret` in `config/deploy.yml`. Keep these keys stable across deploys, too.
+
+## Deploying updates and looking after data
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal deploy  # Build and deploy the latest committed code
+bin/kamal logs    # Follow application and background job logs
+bin/kamal console
+bin/kamal shell
+```
+
+Solid Queue runs inside Puma, so there is no separate jobs role or container to start. `WEB_CONCURRENCY` and `JOB_CONCURRENCY` both default to one in this config; increase them only as the server's resources allow.
+
+The named Docker volume **`fizzy_storage`** is mounted at **`/rails/storage`**. It contains:
+
+- `production.sqlite3` — application data
+- `production_queue.sqlite3`, `production_cache.sqlite3`, and `production_cable.sqlite3` — jobs, cache, and broadcasts
+- `production/files/` — uploaded files, including attachments and exports
+
+Normal deploys replace the app container but reuse this volume. Do not rename the volume or mount, delete it, or prune it when it is unused. A Docker volume survives a deploy, **not** the loss of the server.
+
+Back up the entire volume off-server and test restores. Stop the app (and therefore its jobs) with `bin/kamal app stop` for a consistent filesystem backup, or use SQLite-aware backup tooling; blindly copying live SQLite files can miss writes in WAL files. Start the app again with `bin/kamal app start` after a stopped backup. Keep a separate secure backup of `.kamal/secrets`. This configuration does not provide automatic backups or high availability.
diff --git a/test/lib/deployment_configuration_test.rb b/test/lib/deployment_configuration_test.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e882a13
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/lib/deployment_configuration_test.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,173 @@
+require "test_helper"
+require "kamal"
+require "open3"
+require "tmpdir"
+
+class DeploymentConfigurationTest < ActiveSupport::TestCase
+  test "Kamal deploys one self-contained app behind the TLS proxy" do
+    config = deployment_config
+
+    assert_equal [ "web" ], config.roles.map(&:name)
+    assert_equal 1, config.app_hosts.size
+    assert_equal config.app_hosts, config.proxy.hosts
+    assert config.proxy.ssl?
+    assert_equal 80, config.proxy.app_port
+    assert_empty config.accessories
+    assert config.registry.local?
+    assert_equal "Dockerfile", config.builder.dockerfile
+    assert_equal [ "fizzy_storage:/rails/storage" ], config.raw_config.volumes
+    assert_equal "/rails/public/assets", config.raw_config.asset_path
+
+    assert_equal "false", config.env.clear["SAAS"]
+    assert_equal "production", config.env.clear["RAILS_ENV"]
+    assert_equal "sqlite", config.env.clear["DATABASE_ADAPTER"]
+    assert_equal "local", config.env.clear["ACTIVE_STORAGE_SERVICE"]
+    assert_equal "true", config.env.clear["SOLID_QUEUE_IN_PUMA"]
+    assert_equal config.app_hosts.first, config.env.clear["APP_FQDN"]
+    assert_equal 1, config.env.clear["WEB_CONCURRENCY"]
+    assert_equal 1, config.env.clear["JOB_CONCURRENCY"]
+    assert_equal %w[ SECRET_KEY_BASE SMTP_USERNAME SMTP_PASSWORD ], config.env.secret_keys
+  end
+
+  test "secrets template supplies app secrets without expanding literal passwords" do
+    Dir.mktmpdir do |directory|
+      path = File.join(directory, "secrets")
+      template = Rails.root.join(".kamal/secrets.example").read
+      template.sub!("replace-with-output-of-bin-rails-secret", "deployment-test-only")
+      template.sub!("replace-with-your-smtp-username", "mail-user")
+      template.sub!("replace-with-your-smtp-password", "'mail $password #with spaces'")
+      File.write(path, template)
+
+      env = deployment_config(secrets_path: path).env.to_h
+      assert_equal "deployment-test-only", env["SECRET_KEY_BASE"]
+      assert_equal "mail-user", env["SMTP_USERNAME"]
+      assert_equal "mail $password #with spaces", env["SMTP_PASSWORD"]
+
+      File.write(path, "SECRET_KEY_BASE=deployment-test-only\n")
+      assert_raises Kamal::ConfigurationError do
+        deployment_config(secrets_path: path).env.to_h
+      end
+    end
+  end
+
+  test "production uses the public HTTPS hostname and configured SMTP server" do
+    settings = production_settings
+    urls = { "host" => "fizzy.example.test", "protocol" => "https" }
+
+    assert_equal urls, settings["routes"]
+    assert_equal urls, settings["mailer_urls"]
+    assert_equal urls, settings["controller_urls"]
+    assert settings["assume_ssl"]
+    assert settings["force_ssl"]
+    assert_equal 200, settings["health_status"]
+    assert_equal "Fizzy <fizzy@example.test>", settings["from"]
+    assert_equal "smtp", settings["delivery_method"]
+    assert_equal({
+      "address" => "smtp.example.test", "port" => 587, "domain" => "example.test",
+      "user_name" => "mail-user", "password" => "test-password", "authentication" => "plain",
+      "enable_starttls_auto" => true, "tls" => false
+    }, settings["smtp"].slice("address", "port", "domain", "user_name", "password", "authentication", "enable_starttls_auto", "tls"))
+
+    assert_equal "solid_queue", settings["queue_adapter"]
+    assert_equal %w[ cable cache primary queue ], settings["databases"].keys.sort
+    settings["databases"].each_value do |database|
+      assert_equal "sqlite3", database["adapter"]
+      assert_match %r{\Astorage/production(?:_\w+)?\.sqlite3\z}, database["database"]
+    end
+    assert_equal Rails.root.join("storage/production/files").to_s, settings["uploads"]
+  end
+
+  test "SMTP defaults to STARTTLS on port 587 and uses the public hostname for HELO" do
+    settings = production_settings("SMTP_PORT" => nil, "SMTP_DOMAIN" => nil, "SMTP_AUTHENTICATION" => nil,
+      "SMTP_ENABLE_STARTTLS_AUTO" => nil, "SMTP_TLS" => nil)
+
+    assert_equal 587, settings["smtp"]["port"]
+    assert_equal "fizzy.example.test", settings["smtp"]["domain"]
+    assert_equal "plain", settings["smtp"]["authentication"]
+    assert settings["smtp"]["enable_starttls_auto"]
+    assert_equal false, settings["smtp"]["tls"]
+  end
+
+  test "implicit SMTP TLS disables STARTTLS" do
+    settings = production_settings("SMTP_PORT" => "465", "SMTP_TLS" => "true", "SMTP_AUTHENTICATION" => "login")
+
+    assert_equal 465, settings["smtp"]["port"]
+    assert_equal "login", settings["smtp"]["authentication"]
+    assert settings["smtp"]["tls"]
+    assert_equal false, settings["smtp"]["enable_starttls_auto"]
+  end
+
+  test "SMTP supports an unauthenticated relay" do
+    settings = production_settings("SMTP_PORT" => "25", "SMTP_USERNAME" => "", "SMTP_PASSWORD" => "",
+      "SMTP_AUTHENTICATION" => "", "SMTP_ENABLE_STARTTLS_AUTO" => "false")
+
+    assert_equal 25, settings["smtp"]["port"]
+    assert_nil settings["smtp"]["user_name"]
+    assert_nil settings["smtp"]["password"]
+    assert_nil settings["smtp"]["authentication"]
+    assert_equal false, settings["smtp"]["enable_starttls_auto"]
+  end
+
+  test "HTTP-only production still respects DISABLE_SSL" do
+    settings = production_settings("DISABLE_SSL" => "true")
+
+    assert_equal "http", settings["routes"]["protocol"]
+    assert_equal "http", settings["mailer_urls"]["protocol"]
+    assert_equal false, settings["assume_ssl"]
+    assert_equal false, settings["force_ssl"]
+    assert_equal 200, settings["health_status"]
+  end
+
+  test "image builds can boot without deployment settings or real secrets" do
+    settings = production_settings("APP_FQDN" => nil, "SMTP_ADDRESS" => nil,
+      "SECRET_KEY_BASE" => nil, "SECRET_KEY_BASE_DUMMY" => "1")
+
+    assert_empty settings["routes"]
+    assert_empty settings["mailer_urls"]
+    assert_equal "localhost", settings["smtp"]["address"]
+    assert_equal 25, settings["smtp"]["port"]
+    assert_equal 200, settings["health_status"]
+  end
+
+  private
+    def deployment_config(**overrides)
+      config = Kamal::Configuration.load_raw_config(config_file: Rails.root.join("config/deploy.yml"))
+      Kamal::Configuration.new(config.merge(overrides), version: "deployment-test")
+    end
+
+    def production_settings(overrides = {})
+      env = {
+        "SAAS" => "false", "RAILS_ENV" => "production", "DATABASE_ADAPTER" => "sqlite",
+        "ACTIVE_STORAGE_SERVICE" => "local", "SECRET_KEY_BASE" => "deployment-test-only",
+        "SECRET_KEY_BASE_DUMMY" => nil, "RAILS_MASTER_KEY" => nil,
+        "APP_FQDN" => "fizzy.example.test", "MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS" => "Fizzy <fizzy@example.test>",
+        "SMTP_ADDRESS" => "smtp.example.test", "SMTP_PORT" => "587", "SMTP_DOMAIN" => "example.test",
+        "SMTP_USERNAME" => "mail-user", "SMTP_PASSWORD" => "test-password", "SMTP_AUTHENTICATION" => "plain",
+        "SMTP_ENABLE_STARTTLS_AUTO" => "true", "SMTP_TLS" => "false",
+        "DISABLE_SSL" => nil, "ASSUME_SSL" => nil, "FORCE_SSL" => nil
+      }.merge(overrides)
+
+      script = <<~RUBY
+        require "json"
+        require "rack/mock"
+        puts JSON.generate(
+          routes: Rails.application.routes.default_url_options,
+          mailer_urls: ActionMailer::Base.default_url_options,
+          controller_urls: ActionController::Base.default_url_options,
+          smtp: ActionMailer::Base.smtp_settings,
+          from: ApplicationMailer.default[:from],
+          delivery_method: ActionMailer::Base.delivery_method,
+          assume_ssl: Rails.application.config.assume_ssl,
+          force_ssl: Rails.application.config.force_ssl,
+          health_status: Rack::MockRequest.new(Rails.application).get("/up", "HTTP_HOST" => "fizzy.example.test").status,
+          queue_adapter: ActiveJob::Base.queue_adapter_name,
+          databases: ActiveRecord::Base.configurations.configs_for(env_name: "production").to_h { |db| [db.name, db.configuration_hash.slice(:adapter, :database)] },
+          uploads: ActiveStorage::Blob.service.root.to_s
+        )
+      RUBY
+
+      output, error, status = Open3.capture3(env, "bin/rails", "runner", script, chdir: Rails.root.to_s)
+      assert status.success?, "Production boot failed:\n#{output}\n#{error}"
+      JSON.parse(output.lines.last)
+    end
+end
